> > > > >
> > > > > On Tue, Feb 18, 2020 at 2:41 PM Ben Augustine <baug...@vt.edu> wrote:
> > > > > > Actually, a decent solution in this case is for the user to supply one proposal parameter for the activity centers and make sure the acceptance rates for the marked individuals is OK. Absent a major model specification, the unmarked activity center acceptance rates will necessarily be at least decent. But that rule of thumb isn't available for similar models with no marked individuals. In either case, we shouldn't let nimble select or tune it.
