Hi Nimble Users,

I have recently switched over to using Nimble and I want to do some model comparisons. I feel like I must be missing something very obvious but I can't see a way to extract or calculate the deviance using Nimble. I cannot see anything mentioned in the user manual or any previous threads here.

Would anyone be able to point me in the right direction? I can calculate the log likelihood prior to MCMC using $calculate but I am looking for a way to calculate deviance from the completed MCMC samples or summary.

Thank you,

Emily

